/Title (As the month of Divine Mercy and Forgiveness, it is a most opportune time for teshuvah \("return" to G-d\), prayer, charity, and increased Ahavat Yisrael \(love for a fellow Jew\) in the quest for self-improvement and coming closer to G-d. Chassidic master Rabbi Schneur Zalman of Liadi likens the month of Elul to a time when "the king is in the field" and, in contrast to when he is in the royal palace, "everyone who so desires is permitted to meet him, and he receives them all with a cheerful  ```````````)
